Because we updated the backend to create every batch in an **'S' (Saved/Draft)** state, we now have a slight trap on the frontend!
Currently, if the Maker clicks the **"Execute Immediately"** button on the final success screen, your React code just resets the page (handleResetWizard). It never tells the backend that the user is done! As a result, the batch will stay trapped in the 'S' state forever, and Checkers will never see it.
We need to create a function that explicitly calls the /JS/voucher/update-schedule API with a blank time, triggering our new "Double-Lock" backend logic to flip the switch to 'P'.
Here are the three quick changes you need to make in **VoucherPosting.jsx**.
### 1. Add the Loading State
Find your wizard states near the top of the file (around line 90) and add a loading state for the immediate execution button:
**FIND THIS:**
```javascript
  const [showSchedulePicker, setShowSchedulePicker] = useState(false);
  const [isApplyingSchedule, setIsApplyingSchedule] = useState(false);

```
**ADD THIS RIGHT BELOW IT:**
```javascript
  const [isExecutingImmediately, setIsExecutingImmediately] = useState(false);

```
### 2. Add the handleExecuteImmediately Function
Find your existing handleApplySchedule function (around line 210). Right **below** that entire function, paste this new one:
```javascript
  const handleExecuteImmediately = async () => {
    setIsExecutingImmediately(true);
    try {
      // Sending a null/empty scheduledTime tells the backend to just run the status flip logic
      await callApi("/JS/voucher/update-schedule", {
        batchId: submittedBatchId,
        scheduledTime: null 
      }, "POST");

      showSnackBar("Request submitted for immediate execution!", "success");
      handleResetWizard();
    } catch (e) {
      showSnackBar(e.message || "Failed to finalize batch execution.", "error");
    } finally {
      setIsExecutingImmediately(false);
    }
  };

```
### 3. Wire Up the "Execute Immediately" Button
Scroll all the way down to Step 3 (around line 690) where the two large buttons are rendered. We need to swap out the onClick handler and add the loading spinner.
**FIND THIS:**
```javascript
