                    // ... onClick logic

```
**REPLACE IT WITH THIS:**
```javascript
              {!showSchedulePicker ? (
                <Box sx={{ display: 'flex', gap: 3, justifyContent: 'center' }}>
                  <Button 
                    variant="outlined" 
                    size="large" 
                    onClick={handleExecuteImmediately} 
                    disabled={isExecutingImmediately || isApplyingSchedule}
                    sx={jpStyles.largeBtn}
                  >
                    {isExecutingImmediately ? <CircularProgress size={24} color="inherit" /> : "Execute Immediately"}
                  </Button>
                  <Button
                    variant="contained"
                    size="large"
                    startIcon={<ScheduleIcon />}
                    // ... onClick logic remains the same

```
Now, whether the Maker sets a future schedule or clicks "Execute Immediately", the frontend explicitly contacts the backend, triggering your new, highly secure double-lock logic!
